OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real,
compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by every DONE
sibling page (ActionBuilder, AutomationsListPage, AutomationActivityFeedPage, ApiPlaygroundPage, …
all under Sources/Features/<Domain>). `Sources` is a project.yml source path
(createIntermediateGroups), shared by the iOS + macOS app targets (ADR-002). The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Automations`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only
deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9 (identical to the
DONE sibling ActionBuilder's reconciliation).

REUSE / DRY (engineering principles — no duplication of the proven domain core):
The pure, Foundation-only projection layer for this surface already ships, module-public, in the
P4 feature-view (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/ConditionBuilder.{Types,Adapter,Model}.swift`):
the discriminated `ConditionBody` union + the four `*Condition` structs + `AutomationConditionInput`,
the option enums (`AutomationConditionKind`/`…SignalOp`/`AutomationGeofenceState`/
`AutomationOtherAutomationState`), the `SignalField` catalog, `ConditionBuilderAdapter`
(`defaultCondition`/`signalChanged`/`operatorChanged`/`signalValueFromInput`/`signalValueString`/
`numericValue`/`parseFloatOrZero`/`parseIntOrZero`/`withNumber|Min|Max|Bool`/`toggleDay`/
`timezoneSelection`/`geofenceSelection`/`geofencePlaceId`/`operators`/`isBoolSignal`), and the
geofence state-holder (`GeofenceOption`, `GeofenceLoadState`, `GeofencePresentation`,
`GeofenceOptionsModel`, `GeofenceOptionsSource`, `InMemoryGeofenceOptionsSource`). This unit REUSES
that core (one source of truth, zero type collisions — new symbols are all `ConditionBuilderPage*`)
and feeds it a `Localizable.xcstrings` localizer, then ships a fresh page/model/views that resolve
every string from the platform catalog (the P7 string requirement). NO feature-views file was
edited (out of allowed scope).

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `ConditionBuilder` is a composable SECTION the `/automations` builder page renders inline —
NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level `AppRoute` (that would hijack a
sibling unit's route). Instead it ships a typed `NavigationDestination` seam —
`ConditionBuilderPageLink` + `View.conditionBuilderDestination()` +
`ConditionBuilderPageRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that any `NavigationStack` adopts to deep-link
the full-screen editor. No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) were made —
correct for an unrouted unit (covenant #7).

